	⟪(2)⟫ emphatic, ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫ (M, Pr., 86; Bl., § 48, 1, 2, 7), ⟦Matthew 1:21|Mt 1:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:50|12:50⟧, ⟦Luke 6:35|Lk 6:35⟧, al.; pointing to some one as master (cl.), ⟦Matthew 8:24|Mt 8:24⟧, ⟦Mark 4:38|Mk 4:38⟧, al.; αὐ., καὶ αὐ. = οὗτος, ὁ δε (Bl., § 48, 1), ⟦Matthew 14:2|Mt 14:2⟧, ⟦Mark 14:15|Mk 14:15⟧, ⟦Mark 14:44|44⟧, ⟦Luke 1:22|Lk 1:22⟧ ⟦Luke 2:28|2:28⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ In oblique cases (cl.), for the simple pron. of 3rd pers., ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫, ⟦Matthew 7:9|Mt 7:9⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:12|10:12⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:44|26:44⟧, al.; with ptcp. in gen. absol., ⟦Matthew 9:18|Mt 9:18⟧, ⟦Mark 13:1|Mk 13:1⟧, al. (for irreg. constructions, V. Bl., § 74, 5); pleonastically after the relative (cf. Heb. ⁨אֲשֶׁר לֹו⁩; WM, 184 ff.; Bl., § 50, 4; MM, s.v.), ⟦Mark 7:25|Mk 7:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:8|Re 3:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:2|7:2⟧, al.; in constr. ad sensum, without proper subject expressly indicated, ⟦Matthew 4:23|Mt 4:23⟧, ⟦Acts 8:5|Ac 8:5⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:13|II Co 2:13⟧, al.; gen. αὐτοῦ = ἐκείνου, ⟦Romans 11:11|Ro 11:11⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|I Th 2:19⟧, ⟦Titus 3:5|Tit 3:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:4|He 2:4⟧.
⟪3.⟫ ὁ, ἡ, τὸ αὐ., ⟪the same⟫: ⟦Hebrews 1:12|He 1:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:8|13:8⟧; τὸ αὐ., ποιεῖν, ⟦Matthew 5:46|Mt 5:46⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:47|47⟧, al.; φρονεῖν, ⟦Romans 12:16|Ro 12:16⟧ ⟦Romans 15:5|15:5⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:2|Phl 2:2⟧, al.; τὰ αὐ., ⟦Acts 15:27|Ac 15:27⟧, ⟦Romans 2:1|Ro 2:1⟧, al.; κατὰ τὸ (τὰ) αὐ. (MM, s.v.), ⟦Acts 14:1|Ac 14:1⟧, ⟦Luke 6:23|Lk 6:23⟧, al.; ἐπὶ τὸ αὐ., ⟪together⟫ (MM, s.v.), ⟦Matthew 22:34|Mt 22:34⟧, ⟦Acts 1:15|Ac 1:15⟧, al.; ἓν κ. τὸ αὐ., ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:11|12:11⟧; c. dat. (cl.), ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧; with a noun, λόγος, Mk 14:39; μέτρος, ⟦Philippians 1:30|Phl 1:30⟧; πνεῦμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:4|I Co 12:4⟧.

